    <string name="journal_log_1">Waterline still wet. Her stride lengthened at the ford.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_2">Four nests in nine paces. We went around.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_3">Rain filled the pugmarks before noon; the ridge kept the shape.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_4">She circled twice here, then chose the northern slope.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_5">Claw marks at shoulder height. Territory, not warning.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_6">Counted eight coils. Counted them twice. Walked the rim.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_7">The stones remember nothing. The mud across them does.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_8">Fresh prints over last night\'s rain. We are close now.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_9">Porter\'s hide tent, shredded, abandoned. No blood.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_10">Nine clean bands on the flank, seen at forty paces.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_11">Grass bent in a single line. Something heavy, unhurried.</string>
    <string name="journal_log_12">Here the trail ends and the journal is whole.</string>
